# Your settings for Kamerplanter. A value here wins over the defaults in
# /usr/share/kamerplanter/kamerplanter.env and over the secrets generated
# in /etc/kamerplanter/secrets.env. This file survives updates and rollbacks.
#
# One KEY=VALUE per line, taken literally (no quotes are removed).
# Apply a change with:  systemctl restart kamerplanter.target
#
# Three values must not change once Kamerplanter has stored data; the
# appliance refuses to start if they do:
#   ERASURE_TOMBSTONE_SALT  keys the records of deleted accounts, never change
#   FERNET_KEY              encrypts stored credentials
#   ARANGODB_PASSWORD       the database keeps its first password; change it
#                           in the database first
# Back up /etc/kamerplanter/secrets.env together with your data.
#
# Examples:
# CORS_ORIGINS=["https://kamerplanter.example.org"]
# FRONTEND_URL=https://kamerplanter.example.org
# REGISTRATION_MODE=invite_only
